components.responsibility:
Go literal tables.
- sources []source{Name, Edition, Assertions}. A ledger body is named "ledger:<epic id>/<file>", with Edition the sha256 of the body text exactly as SELECTed. An in-tree file is named by its path, with Edition the git blob id at 845585a.
- rows []row{ID, Source, At, Says, Kind, By, Via, Why}. Kind is Ported, Verbatim, Helper, Amended or Superseded.

TestPortedAssertionsHaveAGoTest calls check(sources, rows, repoRoot) and fails on each problem it returns. The checker uses go/parser only and never the environment or the ledger. It checks:
(a) IDs are unique, (Source, At) pairs are unique, and every Source is declared;
(b) each source's row count equals its Assertions;
(c) a Ported row's By is '<dir>.<Func>' naming a top-level func in that directory, with a `ported:<ID>` comment inside the func's span; when Func is not Test*, Via names an existing Test* under tests/acceptance;
(d) a Verbatim row's By names the body's test func, and the committed file's sha256 (CRLF to LF) equals the source's Edition;
(e) a Helper row's By names an existing Test* in internal/testutil/headless or internal/testutil/program, and has a Why;
(f) an Amended row has a Why, and its By, when given, satisfies (c);
(g) a Superseded row has a Why and no By;
(h) every `ported:` tag under tests/acceptance and internal/testutil/program has a row.

TestPortedCheckerRefusesGaps feeds check broken tables (a missing row, a wrong count, a Ported row without a tag, a stray tag, an Amended row without a Why, a Verbatim row with a wrong edition) and asserts each is reported.

The sources are:
- the six Python bodies (rows per assertion site);
- the ten Go bodies (one Verbatim or Amended row each);
- run_finish_e004_2.py: chrome() exits are Helper rows to Browser's skip tests; the ROOT and browser-list patch checks and the no-Edge check are Amended (no patching: the browser comes only from Open); seed L108/L121/L127 and look L221 and L245-247 are Ported; the watchdog is Superseded by the 30 s CDP deadlines;
- run_finish.py: BASELINE is Superseded by go test ./... and E-009 line 4; edge_risk is a Helper row to the Edge tests; read_bodies' checks are Superseded runner machinery;
- check_run_finish_needs_chrome_bin.py and test_run_finish_edge_guard.py: Helper rows to headless's CHROME_BIN and Edge tests;
- serve_show_all.py: build succeeds is Ported to Build, /healthz 200 is Ported to Start;
- check_e006_1_stops_at_block.py: pass outright is Ported to TestE006RemovalAndPlaceholders; stops at the 404 is Superseded because SC-021 shipped (#976, spike 3).

`//go:build sc042breaks`. TestBrokenProgramsFailTheirAcceptanceTests finds the module root with `go env GOMOD`. It has a table of breaks, each {name, table, ddl, pkg, test}:
- gate (sessions, every new session made the owner's) for e001_1_owner_only_admin.TestE001OwnerOnlyAdmin;
- opens (report_opens, AFTER INSERT delete by report_id/day/visitor, since it is WITHOUT ROWID) for e002_3_opens_counted_once.TestE002OpensCountedOnce;
- likes (votes) for e003_1.TestE003SignInAndVote;
- flatten (comments, AFTER INSERT WHEN NEW.parent_id IS NOT NULL set parent_id NULL) for e004_1.TestE004CommentsAndReplies;
- feedback (feedback, AFTER INSERT delete by id) for e005_1.TestE005PrivateFeedback;
- placeholder (comments.removed_at undone) for e006_1.TestE006RemovalAndPlaceholders;
- blocked (blocked_accounts, AFTER INSERT delete) for e006_2.TestE006BlockingAndUnblocking.
The gate, likes, placeholder and blocked DDL are E-009 line 5's own.

For each break it does four things.
(1) It runs `go test -count=1 -v -run ^<test>$ ./tests/acceptance/<pkg>` as is, and requires exit 0 and '--- PASS: <test>'.
(2) In a space-free MkdirTemp it writes line 5's break source (a goroutine started in init that installs the trigger once the table exists, then writes a mark) and an overlay that adds it to cmd/hband. It confirms the overlay compiles with go build.
(3) It runs the same command with GOFLAGS = the inherited flags minus -tags, plus -overlay=<json>.
(4) It requires exit 1, '--- FAIL: <test>', and the mark file. No mark means the break was never met, which differs from a test that missed the break.
Nothing is written into the repository.
